  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1018 PM MDT Mon Sep 7 2026\n\nDrier southwesterly flow will gradually transition to more zonal \nflow by Wednesday as high pressure builds into the Desert Southwest. \nAs a result, generally clear skies and warming temperatures will be \nthe story for the coming week. There is a low (<15%) chance for an \nisolated shower or thunderstorm over the San Juans and Divide each \nafternoon. Temperatures will run 5-10 degrees above normal through \nthe rest of the work week, with potential to drop back to near \nnormal values over the weekend. Guidance is hinting at a potential \nmoisture return at that point, as a trough moves into the Pacific \nNorthwest and pushes the high to the east. However, agreement on \nthis solution is still somewhat poor, so stay tuned if you have\nplans this coming weekend. In the meantime, enjoy the pleasant \nlate summer/early fall conditions.",
